|> Exercise
    handle=_construct_signature_impossible_

    Can one construct a function of signature $$[\s] \ra [\te{kg}]$$
    from functions
    $f : [\s] \ra [\m]$, $g : [\te{kg}^2] \ra [\te{kg}]$?

    |> Solution
        👎
        It is impossible to manufacture a kilogram
        out of thin air: the only thing that can come
        upstream of $g$ is “more $g$”.
        👎

        !! Impossible using the given function operations.
